    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main 16d23d979: the issue's MCP reproduction passes without a change.\n\nSteps of the check:\n- I revolved the issue's two meridians with 48 segments and imported them as STL.\n- I loaded `assets/machines/lathe.mch`, set the stock from the blank model and set `set_raw_stock_only {on: true}`.\n- I made Boring with `BR-1000` on the finished model: clearance 70, top 58, bottom 42, tolerance 0.05, feed 120, plunge feed 40.\n- On 16d23d979, `verify` gives `ok: true` with no findings.\n\nThe likely fix is commit ec2112539 (PR #2911, \"fix(turning): stop reading thread valleys and neck steps as false hidden rest\"). This commit came after the issue's base 58cb641ca.\n\nEvidence: I put back the files of ec2112539^ for `crates/sim/src/solid_rest.rs`, `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan_hidden.rs` and `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/scan_turned.rs`. With those files, the same test fails with the issue's text:\n\n```text\nfinish envelope near move 1: 0.0000 mm gouge, 11.5425 mm rest\n```\n\nSuggest closing; the maintainer decides. I release the claim.\n",
